ime_limit":25},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A second-order equation is linear if it can be written as $x''+a_1(t)x'+a_0(t)x=g(t)$. Which of these equations in $x(t)$ is nonlinear?","options":["$x''+x\\,x'=0$","$x''+t^2x=0$","$x''+x=\\mathrm{e}^{t^2}$","$x''+\\sin(t)\\,x'=0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a9e79516e52e2de50a47622b","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How should the equation $x''+t\\,x'=4x$ for the unknown $x(t)$ be classified, using the form $x''+a_1(t)x'+a_0(t)x=g(t)$?","options":["Linear, inhomogeneous, with forcing $g=4x$","Nonlinear, because of the product $t\\,x'$","Linear, homogeneous, with non-constant coefficients","Linear, homogeneous, with constant coefficients"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2b88efd95eb3eddbfaedea9c","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For $x''+a_1(t)x'+a_0(t)x=g(t)$ with $a_1,a_0,g$ continuous on an interval containing $t_0$, which data fix exactly one solution, whatever values are prescribed?","options":["$x(t_0)=x_0$ alone","$x(t_0)$, $x'(t_0)$ and $x''(t_0)$ all prescribed","$x(t_0)=x_0$ together with $x'(t_1)=v_0$, $t_1\\neq t_0$","$x(t_0)=x_0$ together with $x'(t_0)=v_0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a1b72e03838499034b100b53","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $a_1,a_0$ be continuous on an interval $I$. What is the dimension of the vector space of solutions of $x''+a_1(t)x'+a_0(t)x=0$ on $I$?","options":["Exactly $1$, as for a first-order equation","Infinite, as it is a space of functions","$2$ for constant coefficients, else infinite","Exactly $2$, also for non-constant coefficients"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"27d30f88a64528be2a873fae","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Setting $y_1=x$ and $y_2=x'$ rewrites $x''+5x'+6x=0$ as $\\boldsymbol{y}'=M\\boldsymbol{y}$ with $\\boldsymbol{y}=(y_1,y_2)^{\\top}$. Which matrix is $M$?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\-6&-5\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\-5&-6\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\6&5\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\-6&-5\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"db3658fb29e816ce485ab55e","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"The functions $\\mathrm{e}^{-t}$ and $\\mathrm{e}^{-2t}$ solve $x''+3x'+2x=0$, and every solution is $c_1\\mathrm{e}^{-t}+c_2\\mathrm{e}^{-2t}$. Which solution satisfies $x(0)=1$ and $x'(0)=0$?","options":["$\\mathrm{e}^{-t}$","$-\\mathrm{e}^{-t}+2\\mathrm{e}^{-2t}$","$2\\mathrm{e}^{-t}-\\mathrm{e}^{-2t}$","$2\\mathrm{e}^{-t}+\\mathrm{e}^{-2t}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c02a34f0909a49b1483a5dad","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Solve the initial value problem $x''=6t$ with $x(0)=1$ and $x'(0)=2$.","options":["$x(t)=3t^2+2t+1$","$x(t)=t^3+2t$","$x(t)=t^3+t+2$","$x(t)=t^3+2t+1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7b5d4010c3d200651f970217","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"The equation $2x''+4x'-6x=t$ is to be written in the explicit form $x''=f(t,x,x')$. Which function is $f$?","options":["$f=\\tfrac{t}{2}-2x'+3x$","$f=t-4x'+6x$","$f=\\tfrac{t}{2}+2x'-3x$","$f=\\tfrac{t}{2}-2x'-3x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"47e47508427a21b4b7ec918e","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which function $x(t)$ satisfies $x''+2x'+x=0$ for all $t$? Check by substituting.","options":["$x=t\\mathrm{e}^{-t}$","$x=t\\mathrm{e}^{t}$","$x=\\mathrm{e}^{t}$","$x=t^2\\mathrm{e}^{-t}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"216808a67327b91d7ac2cefd","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Both $x_1(t)=\\sin t$ and $x_2(t)=2\\sin t$ solve $x''+x=0$ and satisfy $x(0)=0$. What does this show?","options":["The uniqueness result fails for $x''+x=0$","The solutions of $x''+x=0$ form a 1-dimensional space","No initial data give a unique solution of $x''+x=0$","The value $x(0)$ alone does not determine a solution"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"da36df527020440c1b3f4785","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For $x''+a_1(t)x'+a_0(t)x=g(t)$ with $g\\not\\equiv0$, why is the set of solutions NOT a vector space, unlike the case $g\\equiv0$?","options":["The zero function is not a solution, since it gives $0=g$","It has solutions only when $a_1$ and $a_0$ are constants","The sum of two solutions solves it with $g$ replaced by $0$","Its solutions need a third constant to account for $g$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b0842840837d2492530fa2f0","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"With $y_1=x$, $y_2=x'$, the equation $x''+ax'+bx=g(t)$ becomes $\\boldsymbol{y}'=M\\boldsymbol{y}+\\boldsymbol{f}(t)$ for the companion matrix $M$. Which vector is $\\boldsymbol{f}(t)$?","options":["$(g(t),\\;0)^{\\top}$","$(0,\\;g(t))^{\\top}$","$(g(t),\\;g(t))^{\\top}$","$(0,\\;-g(t))^{\\top}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"009299f176bc256834d9f3e8","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Consider $x''+\\frac{1}{t-2}x'+x=\\ln t$ with $x(1)=0$ and $x'(1)=1$. On which largest interval does the existence and uniqueness result guarantee exactly one solution?","options":["$(0,\\infty)$","$(0,2)$","$(-\\infty,2)$","$(1,2)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"29bac19475ea754305f1813f","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Writing $x''-x'-2x=0$ as $\\boldsymbol{y}'=M\\boldsymbol{y}$ with $y_1=x$, $y_2=x'$ gives $M=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}$. What are the eigenvalues of $M$?","options":["$-2$ and $1$","$0$ and $1$","$2$ and $-1$","$-1$ and $-2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a5eab429b13065b9b53eb773","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"The solutions of $x''-x=0$ on $\\mathbb{R}$ form a two-dimensional vector space. Which set of functions is a basis of this space?","options":["$\\{\\mathrm{e}^{t},\\,3\\mathrm{e}^{t}\\}$","$\\{\\mathrm{e}^{t},\\,\\mathrm{e}^{2t}\\}$","$\\{\\mathrm{e}^{t},\\,\\mathrm{e}^{-t}\\}$","$\\{\\mathrm{e}^{t},\\,\\mathrm{e}^{-t},\\,\\sinh t\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6232bebb8e6b6bcd256f2212","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"The equation $x''+x\\,x'=0$ has right-hand side $0$. If $x_1$ and $x_2$ are solutions, must $x_1+x_2$ be a solution?","options":["Yes: a zero right-hand side makes it homogeneous","No: the sum leaves the term $x_1x_2'+x_2x_1'$","Yes: its coefficients do not depend on $t$","No: sums of solutions fail for every second-order equation"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"23429ad6fc7c54e8d37a3982","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $a_1,a_0$ be continuous on an interval $I\\ni t_0$, and let $x$ solve $x''+a_1(t)x'+a_0(t)x=0$ on $I$ with $x(t_0)=0$ and $x'(t_0)=0$. What follows?","options":["$x(t)=0$ only on a neighbourhood of $t_0$","$x(t)=0$ for every $t\\in I$","$x(t)=c(t-t_0)^2$ for some constant $c$","Nothing, unless $x''(t_0)$ is also given"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bc469bda1830ad86c6d56ede","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Every solution of $x''+4x=0$ is $x(t)=c_1\\cos2t+c_2\\sin2t$. How many solutions satisfy the two conditions $x(0)=0$ and $x(\\pi/2)=0$?","options":["Exactly one, the zero function","Exactly one nonzero solution, $\\sin2t$","Infinitely many, namely $c\\sin2t$ for any $c$","None, because the conditions contradict"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"069852db132fe08f35cdfb07","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_second_order_differential_equation_cd224ce4_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Every solution of $x''+x=0$ is $x(t)=c_1\\cos t+c_2\\sin t$. Which solution satisfies $x(\\pi)=2$ and $x'(\\pi)=1$?","options":["$x(t)=2\\cos t+\\sin t$","$x(t)=-2\\cos t-\\sin t$","$x(t)=-2\\cos t+\\sin t$","$x(t)=2\\cos t-\\sin t$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b88d85f2afaf6842e9ba94bb","time_limit":40}]}}